## How It Works

```
Input text
    │
    ▼
┌──────────────────────────┐
│  iterate lines           │
│  ┌─ starts with '#'  ──►│── Header { level, text }
│  ├─ starts with '-'/'*'►│── ListItem(text)
│  ├─ matches "key: val" ►│── MetaData { key, value }
│  ├─ empty line         ►│── BlankLine
│  └─ anything else      ►│── Paragraph(text)
└──────────────────────────┘
    │
    ▼
Document { elements: Vec<Element> }
```

## Key Design Points

| Aspect | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Enums** | `Element` models every line type; `ParseError` models every failure mode |
| **Error handling** | Returns `Result<Document, ParseError>` — no panics |
| **Convenience API** | `headers()`, `list_items()`, `meta(key)` for quick queries |
| **Round-trip** | `to_plain_text()` re-serializes back to the original format |
| **Tests** | 14 tests covering happy path, edge cases, errors, and round-trip |

