## Bug Summary Table

| # | Bug | Fix Applied |
|---|-----|-------------|
| 1 | No default config — crashes on partial input | `static DEFAULTS` merged with config |
| 2 | No running-state flag | `isRunning` / `isFlushing` guards |
| 3 | `start()` can create duplicate intervals | Early return if `isRunning` |
| 4 | `flush()` not awaited inside `setInterval` | `async` wrapper + `try/catch` |
| 5 | `stop()` discards buffered entries | Final `await this.flush()` on stop |
| 6 | `timer` not reset to `null` on stop | Explicit `this.timer = null` |
| 7 | No input validation on `log()` | Type check + `TypeError` |
| 8 | No timestamp on entries | Auto-add `timestamp` + `id` |
| 9 | Auto-flush not awaited | `.catch()` fire-and-forget pattern |
| 10 | No observability | `metrics` object + `getMetrics()` |
| 11 | Entries **lost** on failed flush | Restored to front of buffer |
| 12 | No fetch timeout | `AbortController` with configurable timeout |
| 13 | No retry logic | Exponential backoff (`_sendWithRetry`) |
| 14 | `JSON.stringify` can throw on circular refs | Wrapped in `try/catch` |
| 15 | Failed entries silently dropped | Entries prepended back to buffer |
| 16 | Unstructured `console.log` | Levelled logging (`info/warn/error`) |
| 17 | No success tracking | `metrics.totalFlushed` / `flushCount` |

> **Key principle:** An audit logger must **never silently lose data**. The retry + rollback pattern ensures entries survive transient failures.

