## Key Concepts

```
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│            Cancellation Flow                       │
├────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                                    │
│  CancellationTokenSource    CancellationToken      │
│  (owner / controller)       (passed to worker)     │
│                                                    │
│   cts.Cancel() ──────────► token.IsCancellationRequested  │
│                             token.ThrowIfCancellationRequested()  │
│                                                    │
├────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  ✅ Cooperative: worker must check the token       │
│  ✅ Thread-safe: can be shared across tasks        │
│  ✅ Composable: link multiple tokens together      │
│  ✅ Timeout:  new CancellationTokenSource(delay)   │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

| Feature | `Task` + `CancellationToken` | `BackgroundWorker` |
|---|---|---|
| **Async/Await** | ✅ Full support | ❌ |
| **Cancellation** | `CancellationToken` | `CancelAsync()` flag |
| **Error handling** | `try/catch`, `AggregateException` | `RunWorkerCompleted` |
| **Composability** | Chain tasks, `WhenAll`, etc. | Single operation |
| **Recommended** | ✅ **Yes** | Legacy only |

> **Tip:** Always use `CancellationToken` — pass it to `HttpClient`, `Stream`, `DbCommand`, and other async APIs for end-to-end cancellation support.

