## Key Design Decisions

```
┌──────────┐     ┌─────────┐     ┌──────────┐     ┌───────────────┐
│ Your API │────▸│  Redis   │────▸│  Worker  │────▸│ Elasticsearch │
│ (producer)│    │ (BullMQ) │     │ (batched)│     │               │
└──────────┘     └─────────┘     └──────────┘     └───────────────┘
                                      │
                                 Flush every 2s
                                 or every 50 docs
```

| Concern | Approach |
|---|---|
| **Throughput** | Docs are buffered and bulk-indexed (50 docs or every 2s) |
| **Retries** | Exponential backoff, 5 attempts via BullMQ |
| **Backpressure** | `concurrency: 10` limits parallel processing |
| **Data loss** | Jobs persist in Redis until acknowledged |
| **Graceful shutdown** | Drains in-flight jobs, flushes pending batches |
| **Observability** | Structured logging (pino), failed job events |
| **Schema management** | Indices auto-created on startup with mappings |

