# index some documents
node index.js add blog1 "Introduction to Node.js streams and buffers"
node index.js add blog2 "Building REST APIs with Express and Node.js"
node index.js add blog3 "Python async programming with asyncio"
node index.js add blog4 "JavaScript promises and async await patterns"

# search
node index.js search "node.js async"
node index.js search "REST API"

# manage
node index.js list
node index.js stats
node index.js remove blog3
node index.js clear
```

## Key design decisions

| Area | Choice | Reason |
|---|---|---|
| **Scoring** | TF-IDF | Standard, effective for keyword search |
| **Storage** | Single JSON file | Zero dependencies, inspectable by hand |
| **Tokenizer** | Lowercase + punctuation strip + stop words | Good enough baseline without stemming |
| **Dependencies** | None | Only Node.js built-ins (`fs`, `path`) |

The inverted index maps every unique term to its posting list (array of document IDs). On search, it walks each query token's posting list, accumulates TF-IDF scores per document, and returns results sorted by relevance.

