## Key Design Decisions

| Concern | Solution |
|---|---|
| **Duplicate processing** | Files moved to `processing/` before work begins |
| **Incomplete uploads** | `awaitWriteFinish` waits for file stability |
| **Crash recovery** | Files in `processing/` on restart = manual review |
| **Backpressure** | Bounded concurrency with `maxConcurrent` queue |
| **Transient failures** | Exponential-backoff retry before moving to `failed/` |
| **Graceful shutdown** | Drains active jobs on SIGINT/SIGTERM |
| **New formats** | Drop a new processor in `processors/` and register it |

The pipeline follows the **inbox → processing → reports/failed** pattern used in production ETL systems. Adding a new file format means writing one

