## How It Works

| Component | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `fs.watch()` | Triggers on file changes |
| `lastSize` tracking | Reads only **new bytes** (no reprocessing) |
| `checkBannedWords` | Substring match against a blocklist |
| `checkExcessiveCaps` | Flags messages over 70% uppercase |
| `checkMessageLength` | Rejects oversized messages |
| `checkSpam` | Per-user cooldown via timestamps |
| `flagged.log` | Persistent record of violations |

Each check is independent — a single message can trigger multiple violations. The watcher only reads newly appended content so it stays efficient on large log files.

