## How Retry Flow Works

```
Send batch ──→ Success ──→ Done ✅
     │
     └──→ Fail (5xx / 429)
              │
              ├─ Attempt 1 → wait ~1s  → retry
              ├─ Attempt 2 → wait ~2s  → retry
              ├─ Attempt 3 → wait ~4s  → retry
              └─ All failed → Dead-Letter Queue 🪦

     └──→ Fail (4xx) → Non-retryable → DLQ immediately
```

## Key Design Decisions

| Feature | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Exponential backoff** | `baseDelay × 2^attempt` prevents thundering herd |
| **Jitter** | Random offset avoids synchronized retries from multiple clients |
| **Batching** | Groups logs to reduce HTTP overhead |
| **Dead-letter queue** | Failed logs aren't lost — can be inspected or replayed |
| **Non-retryable errors** | 4xx errors (except 429) skip retry to avoid pointless loops |
| **Graceful shutdown** | Flushes remaining queue before process exits |

