## Architecture Overview

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                  MigrationHelper                     │
│                                                      │
│  reader()  ──►  transformer()  ──►  writer(batch)   │
│  (async gen)     (per record)       (batched)        │
│       │               │                 │            │
│       ▼               ▼                 ▼            │
│  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐   │
│  │             MetricsCollector                  │   │
│  │                                               │   │
│  │  counters:    records.read, .written, .failed │   │
│  │  gauges:      batch.currentSize               │   │
│  │  histograms:  transform (p50/p95/p99)         │   │
│  │               writeBatch (p50/p95/p99)        │   │
│  │  buckets:     writes-per-second throughput     │   │
│  └──────────────────────────────────────────────┘   │
│  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐   │
│  │             ErrorJournal                      │   │
│  │                                               │   │
│  │  categoryCounts:  { transform: N, write: M }  │   │
│  │  entries[]:       capped sample of failures   │   │
│  └──────────────────────────────────────────────┘   │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

## What the Report Contains

| Section | Metrics | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| **records** | `read`, `transformed`, `written`, `skipped`, `failed` | Reconciliation totals |
| **batches** | `total`, `retried` | Write reliability |
| **timing.transform** | `min`, `max`, `mean`, `median`, `p95`, `p99` | Per-record latency distribution |
| **timing.writeBatch** | Same percentiles | Per-batch write latency |
| **throughput** | `avgPerSecond`, `peakPerSecond` | Sustained & burst write rates |
| **errors** | `totalErrors`, `byCategory`, `sampleErrors[]` | Debugging failed records |

## Key Design Decisions

- **Async generator reader** — lazily streams records; works with DB cursors, file streams, or API pagination
- **Histogram collection** — stores every observation so percentiles (p95/p99) are exact, not approximated
- **Time-bucketed throughput** — groups writes into 1-second windows for accurate rate calculation
- **Capped error journal** — keeps memory bounded while still capturing root-cause samples
- **Exponential back-off retries** — both transform and write stages retry independently with increasing delays
- **`abort()` support** — allows external cancellation (e.g., on `SIGINT`) while still producing a final report

