## Bug Summary Table

| # | Bug | Location | Fix |
|---|-----|----------|-----|
| 1 | Missing `Clone` on enums/structs shared via `Arc` | `AuditEventKind`, `AuditEvent` | Added `#[derive(Clone)]` |
| 2 | No thread-safe wrapper on shared buffer | `AuditBuffer` field | Wrapped in `Arc<Mutex<>>` |
| 3 | `fn()` pointer can't capture environment | `SchedulerTask::action` | Changed to `Box<dyn Fn + Send>` |
| 4 | No shutdown signal mechanism | `AuditScheduler::running` | Used `Arc<AtomicBool>` |
| 5 | Buffer grows unbounded past capacity | `AuditBuffer::push` | Added capacity check + eviction |
| 6 | `.clone()` instead of `.drain(..)` leaves events | `drain_all()` | Used `.drain(..).collect()` |
| 7 | Raw `{:?}` on `SystemTime` is unreadable | `Display for AuditEvent` | Formatted as UNIX timestamp |
| 8 | `last_run = now()` skips first immediate tick | `add_task` | Set `last_run` to `now - interval` |
| 9 | `&mut self` across threads is not `Send`-safe | `run()`, `record_event()` | Used `Arc<Mutex<>>` for all shared state |
| 10 | `>` instead of `>=` misses exact interval match | Tick comparison | Changed to `>=` |
| 11 | Busy-loop with no sleep burns 100% CPU | `run()` loop | Added `thread::sleep(50ms)` |
| 12 | No final flush on shutdown loses buffered events | End of `run()` | Called

