## Bug Summary Table

| # | Bug | Fix |
|---|-----|-----|
| 1 | Missing `express.json()` middleware | Added body parser with size limit |
| 2 | No input validation | Added `validateDocument()` helper |
| 3 | Loose equality (`==`) for `undefined` | Strict `===` with null checks |
| 4 | Tokenizer only splits on spaces | Regex: remove punctuation, split on `\s+` |
| 5 | Overwrites index entries (`= [id]`) | Uses `Set.add()` to append |
| 6 | Stores object references | Uses `structuredClone()` for deep copy |
| 7 | Double response (no `return` after 400) | Added `return` before error responses |
| 8 | Reads body in GET request | Uses `req.query.q` instead |
| 9 | No empty query handling | Validates before processing |
| 10 | Duplicate results in search | Uses `Map` for dedup + scoring |
| 11 | Returns raw IDs not documents | Returns full documents with `_score` |
| 12 | Delete only removes doc, not tokens | Cleans up inverted index entries |
| 13 | No response sent on DELETE | Sends 200 or 404 response |
| 14 | No global error handler | Added Express error middleware |
| 15 | Hardcoded port | Uses `process.env.PORT` with fallback |

