## Key Design Decisions

| Decision | Reason |
|---|---|
| **`fs.watch` over `fs.watchFile`** | Event-driven, no polling, lower CPU |
| **Debouncing per file path** | Editors trigger multiple saves; avoids duplicate runs |
| **Sequential tasks by default** | Lint → test → build ordering matters |
| **Variable interpolation (`$FILE`)** | Run commands against the specific changed file |
| **Task matching via regex/function/string** | Flexible — match `.js`, `.test.js`, or custom logic |
| **No external dependencies** | Runs on vanilla Node.js 18+ |

The watcher uses Node's native `fs.watch` (inotify on Linux, FSEvents on macOS, ReadDirectoryChangesW on Windows). For production use on Linux where you might hit inotify limits, increase it via `sudo sysctl fs.inotify.max_user_watches=524288`.

