## How It Works

```
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                   MigrationHelper                      │
│                                                        │
│  items ──► chunk into batches                          │
│               │                                        │
│               ▼                                        │
│  ┌─────────────────────────┐                           │
│  │  For each batch:        │                           │
│  │                         │                           │
│  │  1. RateLimiter.acquire │◄── Token Bucket           │
│  │     (wait if needed)    │    (capacity + refill/s)  │
│  │                         │                           │
│  │  2. execute_with_retry  │                           │
│  │     ┌──────────────┐    │                           │
│  │     │ Ok ──────► ✓ │    │                           │
│  │     │ RateLimit ─► │    │                           │
│  │     │   wait then  │    │                           │
│  │     │   re-acquire │    │                           │
│  │     │ Transient ─► │    │                           │
│  │     │   exp backoff│    │                           │
│  │     │ Permanent ─► ✗│   │                           │
│  │     └──────────────┘    │                           │
│  │                         │                           │
│  │  3. ProgressTracker     │                           │
│  │     record & report     │                           │
│  └─────────────────────────┘                           │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

## Key Design Points

| Component | Purpose |
|---|---|
| **`TokenBucket`** | Classic token-bucket algorithm — tokens refill at a steady rate up to a cap, each request consumes tokens |
| **`RateLimiter`** | `Arc<Mutex<…>>` wrapper so the bucket is safely shared across awaits |
| **`RetryPolicy`** | Configurable max attempts, initial & max backoff, exponential multiplier |
| **`execute_with_retry`** | Distinguishes three error kinds: *rate-limited* (uses server hint), *transient* (exponential backoff), *permanent* (no retry) |
| **`ProgressTracker`** | Tracks succeeded / failed / skipped counts and prints items-per-second throughput |
| **`MigrationHelper::run`** | Orchestrates batching → rate-limit acquire → retry loop → progress reporting |

