## Bug Summary Table

| # | Bug | Fix Applied |
|---|-----|-------------|
| 1 | No input validation | Type checking + `id` requirement |
| 2 | `push(array)` nests instead of flattening | `push(...spread)` |
| 3 | `setInterval` swallows async errors | `try/catch` inside async arrow |
| 4 | `this` lost in `function()` callback | Arrow function `() =>` |
| 5 | `stop()` never clears interval | `clearInterval(this.timer)` |
| 6 | No concurrency guard on batch | `isProcessing` lock flag |
| 7 | `slice` doesn't mutate queue | `splice` removes items |
| 8 | `i <= length` off-by-one | `i < length` |
| 9 | `retries` param undefined on first call | Default parameter `= 0` |
| 10 | `undefined < number` → `false` | Initialized retries properly |
| 11 | No delay between retries | Exponential backoff with `sleep()` |
| 12 | Post-increment `retries++` passes old val | `retries + 1` |
| 13 | Failed docs silently lost | `throw` + `failedDocs` array |
| 14 | Missing `Content-Type` header | Added JSON headers |
| 15 | Listeners overwritten | Array-based listener storage |
| 16 | `emit` crashes if no listener | Existence check before call |
| 17 | No failure tracking | `failedCount` + `failedDocs` |

