| # | Bug | Fix |
|---|-----|-----|
| 1 | Missing `express.json()` middleware | Added `app.use(express.json())` |
| 2 | No input validation | Added `validateTaskInput()` helper |
| 3 | `Math.random()` for IDs (collisions) | Use `crypto.randomUUID()` |
| 4 | Date never parsed from string | `new Date(scheduledTime)` with validation |
| 5 | Mixed date formats (`Date.now()` vs ISO) | Consistent `.toISOString()` everywhere |
| 6 | Wrong delay calculation (string − number) | `runAt.getTime() - Date.now()` |
| 7 | No guard against past dates | Check `delay < 0` → return 400 |
| 8 | Timer reference not stored | `timers.set(id, timer)` via `scheduleTask()` |
| 9 | No HTTP status code on creation | `res.status(201)` |
| 10 | GET endpoint used POST method | Changed to `app.get('/tasks/:id')` |
| 11 | No 404 for missing task | Guard clause returning 404 |
| 12 | Returned raw object, no filtering | Return array with optional `?status=` filter |
| 13 | Timer not cleared on delete | `clearScheduledTimer(id)` before delete |
| 14 | No existence check on delete | Check `tasks.has(id)` first |
| 15 | `executeTask` crashes if task deleted | Null-check + try/catch |
| 16 | Recurrence logic missing | Re-schedule via `RECURRENCE_MS` map |
