## Key Design Decisions

```
┌──────────┐     ┌─────────────┐     ┌─────────────────┐     ┌───────────────┐
│ Producer  │────▶│  RabbitMQ   │────▶│  QueueConsumer  │────▶│ Elasticsearch │
│ (API)     │     │  (durable)  │     │  (batch + dedup)│     │  (bulk API)   │
└──────────┘     └─────────────┘     └────────┬────────┘     └───────────────┘
                                              │
                                     retry ◀──┤──▶ DLQ (max retries)
```

| Decision | Why |
|---|---|
| **Batch + flush timer** | Bulk API is far cheaper than per-doc writes; timer ensures low-traffic docs aren't stuck |
| **Deduplication** | Rapid updates to the same doc collapse into one write |
| **Ack before processing** | Decouples queue delivery from ES writes; retries handled internally |
| **Exponential backoff + jitter** | Prevents retry storms when ES is under load |
| **Dead letter queue** | Poison messages don't block the pipeline; inspect and replay later |
| **Graceful shutdown** | Drain the buffer before exit so nothing is silently lost |

