## Key Design Decisions

| Decision | Rationale |
|---|---|
| **Batching with timeout** | ES `_bulk` is far more efficient than single-doc writes; timeout ensures low-volume queues still flush |
| **Per-document error handling** | A bulk request can partially fail — retry only the failed docs instead of the whole batch |
| **DLQ as a separate queue** | Failed jobs stay inspectable and replayable without polluting the main queue |
| **Rate limiter on worker** | Prevents overwhelming ES during spike replays or backfill jobs |
| **`refresh: false`** | Avoids forcing a Lucene segment refresh per batch; let ES handle its own refresh interval |
| **Graceful shutdown** | Drains in-flight jobs and flushes the last batch so nothing is silently lost |

