## Key Design Decisions

| Decision | Rationale |
|---|---|
| **JSONL format** | One record per line — `grep`-able, streamable, easy to ingest into ELK/Splunk/Loki |
| **SHA-256 hashing** | Detects actual content changes vs. metadata-only touches; provides tamper evidence |
| **`awaitWriteFinish`** | Debounces partial writes so you get one `change` event per save, not five |
| **Hash deduplication** | Editors like VS Code trigger multiple writes — skip if hash is unchanged |
| **Stream-based hashing** | Large files don't blow up memory |
| **Log rotation built in** | No dependency on `logrotate`; caps disk usage automatically |
| **`phase` field** | Distinguishes files found at startup (`initial-scan`) from live changes (`watch`) |

