## Bug Summary Table

| # | Bug | Location | Fix |
|---|-----|----------|-----|
| 1 | `std::sync::Mutex` blocks async runtime | State definition | Use `tokio::sync::RwLock` |
| 2 | Missing `Clone` on `AppState` | `struct AppState` | Add `#[derive(Clone)]` + `Arc` wrapping |
| 3 | `Mutex` instead of `RwLock` | State locking | `RwLock` allows concurrent reads |
| 4 | `String` for datetime field | `Task.scheduled_at` | Use `chrono::DateTime<Utc>` |
| 5 | `i32` for retry count (can go negative) | `Task.retries` | Use `u32` for unsigned semantics |
| 6 | Missing `Serialize/Deserialize/Clone` | `enum TaskStatus` | Add all needed derives |
| 7 | No error type — raw strings | Handler returns | `thiserror` enum + `ResponseError` impl |
| 8 | No input validation | `create_task` | `validate()` method on request |
| 9 | `.lock().unwrap()` panics on poison | All handlers | `RwLock` `.read().await` / `.write().await` |
| 10 | Returns `200 OK` on creation | `create_task` | Return `201 Created` |
| 11 | Returns `200` with text on missing task |

