### `TokenBucket.java` — Thread-safe token bucket

```java
package limiter;

/**
 * Token-bucket rate limiter.
 *
 *  - Tokens refill at a constant rate (requestsPerSecond).
 *  - The bucket can hold at most `burstSize` tokens.
 *  - Each request consumes 1 token; if none are available the request is rejected.
 */
public final class TokenBucket {

    private final double refillRate;   // tokens added per nanosecond
    private final int maxTokens;

    private double tokens;
    private long lastRefillNanos;

    public TokenBucket(double requestsPerSecond, int burstSize) {
        this.refillRate     = requestsPerSecond / 1_000_000_000.0;
        this.maxTokens      = burstSize;
        this.tokens         = burstSize;  // start full
        this.lastRefillNanos = System.nanoTime();
    }

    /**
     * Attempts to consume one token.
     * @return true if the request is allowed, false if rate-limited.
     */
    public synchronized boolean tryAcquire() {
        refill();
        if (tokens >= 1.0) {
            tokens -= 1.0;
            return true;
        }
        return false;
    }

    /**
     * Returns the estimated wait time in milliseconds
     * until a token becomes available (0 if available now).
     */
    public synchronized long estimateWaitMs() {
        refill();
        if (tokens >= 1.0) return 0;
        double deficit = 1.0 - tokens;
        return (long) Math.ceil(deficit / (refillRate * 1_000_000));
    }

    private void refill() {
        long now = System.nanoTime();
        double elapsed = now - lastRefillNanos;
        double newTokens = elapsed * refillRate;
        tokens = Math.min(maxTokens, tokens + newTokens);
        lastRefillNanos = now;
    }
}
```

