## Key Design Decisions

| Problem | Solution |
|---|---|
| OS fires duplicate `MODIFY` events | `DebouncedWatchService` deduplicates within a configurable window |
| Blocking `WatchService.take()` | Runs on a dedicated daemon thread, tasks dispatched to a pool |
| Matching files to handlers | Glob-to-regex conversion in `TaskRegistry` (`*.csv`, `config-*.json`) |
| Multiple handlers per file | All matching tasks execute concurrently |
| Task errors killing the watcher | Each task runs in its own `try/catch` in the thread pool |
| Thread cleanup | `AutoCloseable` + daemon threads — won't prevent JVM shutdown |

