## Bug Summary Table

| # | Bug | Fix Applied |
|---|-----|-------------|
| 1 | `List<T>` not thread-safe | → `ConcurrentDictionary` |
| 2 | No cancellation support | → `CancellationTokenSource` |
| 3 | `Timer.Interval = 0` throws | → `Threading.Timer` with valid period |
| 4 | No null check on `AddReport` | → `ArgumentNullException.ThrowIfNull` |
| 5 | Duplicate reports allowed | → `TryAdd` with `Guid` key |
| 6 | Timer never disposed on `Stop()` | → `Change(Infinite)` + `Dispose()` |
| 7 | Re-entrant timer callbacks | → `Interlocked.CompareExchange` guard |
| 8 | Collection modified during `foreach` | → `.ToList()` snapshot |
| 9 | One exception kills all reports | → Per-report `try/catch` |
| 10 | `DateTime.Now` (local time) | → `DateTime.UtcNow` |
| 11 | `.Result` causes deadlock | → `await` async properly |
| 12 | No status/error tracking | → `Status`, `LastRunTimeUtc`, `LastError` |
| 13 | Missing `Hourly`/`Monthly` cases | → Exhaustive `switch` expression |
| 14 | Default returns same time (∞ loop) | → Throw + skip-forward logic |
| 15 | No `IDisposable` | → Full `Dispose` pattern |

---

## Usage Example

```csharp
using Microsoft.Extensions.Logging;

using var loggerFactory = LoggerFactory.Create(b => b.AddConsole());
var logger = loggerFactory.CreateLogger<ReportScheduler>();

using var scheduler = new ReportScheduler(logger, new SampleReportGenerator());

scheduler.AddReport(new ScheduledReport
{
    Name = "Daily Sales",
    Frequency = ScheduleFrequency.Daily,
    NextRunTimeUtc = DateTime.UtcNow.AddSeconds(5)   // first run in 5 s
});

scheduler.AddReport(new ScheduledReport
{
    Name = "Hourly Metrics",
    Frequency = ScheduleFrequency.Hourly,
    NextRunTimeUtc = DateTime.UtcNow.AddSeconds(10)
});

scheduler.Start();
Console.ReadKey();          // keep alive
scheduler.Stop();
```

> **Key takeaways:** Always use **UTC** for scheduling, **await** instead of `.Result`, protect shared state with **thread-safe collections**, and implement **`IDisposable`** for timer-based classes.

