## Key Concepts

| Feature | Method Used |
|---|---|
| **Parse string** | `json::parse(str)` |
| **Parse file** | `file >> jsonObj` |
| **Access value** | `j["key"].get<T>()` |
| **Safe access** | `j.value("key", default)` |
| **Check key exists** | `j.contains("key")` |
| **Iterate array** | `for (auto& item : j)` |
| **Iterate object** | `for (auto& [k, v] : j.items())` |
| **Get type** | `j.type_name()` |

> **Why `nlohmann/json`?** It's header-only (no linking needed), intuitive STL-like syntax, widely adopted, and handles error reporting with exceptions. For performance-critical apps, consider **simdjson** or **rapidjson**.

