> **Key takeaway:** The most critical fixes are the **shared `HttpClient`** (#2), eliminating **`.Result` deadlocks** (#7), and adding **proper error handling** (#8, #10, #13). These three alone account for the majority of production incidents in HTTP-based C# services.

