## Key Concepts Summary

```
Approach              Use Case                       Return Type
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
parseString()         Known structure → typed object  Document (POJO)
parseToTree()         Unknown/dynamic structure       JsonNode (tree)
parseToMap()          Quick key-value access          Map<String, Object>
extractField()        Single field lookup             Optional<String>
extractNestedField()  Dot-notation deep lookup        Optional<String>
toJson()              Serialize back to JSON          String
```

> **Notes:**
> - **Jackson** is the most widely used JSON library in Java (used by Spring Boot)
> - Use **POJO mapping** when your JSON structure is known ahead of time
> - Use **JsonNode tree** when dealing with dynamic/unknown JSON
> - The `ObjectMapper` is **thread-safe** — create it once and reuse it

