```kotlin
// ---------- Entry Point ----------

fun main() = runBlocking {
    // Allow 5 requests/sec, bucket size of 10 (handles small bursts)
    val limiter = TokenBucketRateLimiter(maxTokens = 10, refillRate = 5.0)

    val worker = RateLimitedWorker(
        rateLimiter = limiter,
        maxRetries = 3,
        concurrency = 3,
    )

    // Optional: observe results
    worker.onResult = { result ->
        if (result is TaskResult.Failure) {
            // e.g., push to dead-letter queue
        }
    }

    worker.start()

    // Submit a burst of 15 tasks (exceeds rate → limiter will throttle)
    val jobs = (1..15).map { i ->
        launch {
            val payload = when {
                i == 5  -> "fail-permanent"
                i == 10 -> "fail-transient"
                else    -> "data-item-$i"
            }
            worker.submit(Task(id = "task-$i", payload = payload))
        }
    }
    jobs.joinAll()

    // Let work complete, then shut down
    delay(10_000)
    worker.shutdown()
}
```

## How It Works

```
┌──────────┐       ┌────────────┐       ┌──────────────┐
│ Producer │──send──▶  Channel   │──recv──▶  Worker 0-N  │
│ submit() │       │ (buffered) │       │              │
└──────────┘       └────────────┘       │  ┌────────┐  │
                                        │  │ Rate   │  │
                                        │  │Limiter │  │
                                        │  │acquire │  │
                                        │  └───┬────┘  │
                                        │      ▼       │
                                        │ executeTask()│
                                        │   ↓ retry?   │
                                        └──────┬───────┘
                                               ▼
                                        ┌────────────┐
                                        │  Results   │
                                        │  Channel   │
                                        └────────────┘
```

## Key Design Points

| Concern | Solution |
|---|---|
| **Rate limiting** | Token bucket algorithm — allows short bursts up to `maxTokens`, then throttles to `refillRate`/sec |
| **Backpressure** | Bounded `Channel(capacity)` suspends producers when the queue is full |
| **Concurrency** | Multiple consumer coroutines pull from the same channel (fan-out) |
| **Retries** | Exponential back-off with configurable `maxRetries`; distinguishes retryable vs permanent errors |
| **Graceful shutdown** | `channel.close()` lets consumers drain remaining items, then exit |
| **Thread safety** | `Mutex` protects token state; `AtomicBoolean` guards start/stop |

> **Tip:** For production use, consider adding structured logging, metrics (tokens available, queue depth), and a dead-letter queue for permanently failed tasks. If you need a sliding-window limiter instead of token bucket, swap `TokenBucketRateLimiter` for a `SlidingWindowRateLimiter` with the same `acquire()` interface.

