## All 10 Bugs — Explained & Fixed

| # | Bug | Impact | Fix |
|---|-----|--------|-----|
| 1 | Priority comparator only compares `priority`, ignoring `scheduledTime` | Tasks with equal priority execute in wrong order | Compare time as tie-breaker |
| 2 | `running_` not initialised in init-list | UB — may start as `true` | Initialise to `false` |
| 3 | Destructor doesn't call `stop()` | Threads still joinable → `std::terminate` | Call `stop()` in dtor |
| 4 | `scheduleReport` lacks a lock | Data race on `taskQueue_` | Lock `mtx_` |
| 5 | `generator` copied, not moved | Unnecessary heap traffic | `std::move(generator)` |
| 6 | Worker threads never joined in `stop()` | Joinable threads → UB | Join all workers |
| 7 | Same as 6 (combined fix) | — | — |
| 8 | `getResults()` reads without lock | Data race on `results_` | Lock `mtx_` |
| 9 | `cv_.wait` without predicate | Spurious wake-ups ignored, tasks may stall | Use `wait_for` + predicate |
| 10 | `executeTask` mutates shared state unlocked | Data race on `results_` and `taskQueue_` | Lock around mutations |

