## Key Design Decisions

| Feature | Implementation | Why |
|---|---|---|
| **Thread safety** | `actor` isolation | No manual locks; compiler-enforced data-race safety |
| **Rate limiting** | Token bucket algorithm | Allows bursts up to `capacity` while enforcing a steady-state rate |
| **Backoff** | Exponential + random jitter | Prevents retry storms / thundering-herd |
| **Concurrency cap** | `maxConcurrency` gate in the loop | Limits system resource usage independently of the rate limiter |
| **Result delivery** | `AsyncStream` | Callers consume results asynchronously without tight coupling |
| **Priority** | Sort-on-dequeue | High-priority jobs jump ahead in the queue |
| **Cancellation** | `Task.isCancelled` checks + `CancellationError` | Cooperative cancellation throughout the pipeline |

The **rate limiter** and **concurrency gate** are independent controls — the limiter governs *throughput* (requests/sec) while the gate governs *parallelism* (simultaneous in-flight tasks).

