## How It Fits Together

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                PARENT PROCESS               │
│                                             │
│  pool->cancelAll()                          │
│      │                                      │
│      ├──► posix_kill(pid1, SIGTERM)         │
│      ├──► posix_kill(pid2, SIGTERM)         │
│      └──► pcntl_waitpid(...)                │
└──────┬──────────────────────┬───────────────┘
       │ fork                 │ fork
┌──────▼──────────┐   ┌──────▼──────────┐
│   CHILD 1       │   │   CHILD 2       │
│                 │   │                 │
│ SIGTERM handler │   │ SIGTERM handler │
│   ↓             │   │   ↓             │
│ token->cancel() │   │ token->cancel() │
│   ↓             │   │   ↓             │
│ throwIfCancel() │   │ isCancelled()   │
│ → exception     │   │ → returns true  │
│ → exit(1)       │   │ → cleanup       │
│                 │   │ → exit(1)       │
└─────────────────┘   └─────────────────┘
```

## Key Design Points

| Concern | Solution |
|---|---|
| **Starting work** | `pcntl_fork()` creates an isolated child process |
| **Graceful cancel** | Parent sends `SIGTERM` → child's signal handler calls `token->cancel()` |
| **Force kill** | `SIGKILL` after timeout via `cancelAndWait()` |
| **Responsive sleep** | `sleepWithCancel()` breaks sleep into 100 ms chunks |
| **Two cancellation styles** | `throwIfCancelled()` (exception) or `isCancelled()` (polling) |
| **Cleanup hooks** | `token->onCancel(fn)` runs before the child exits |
| **Zombie prevention** | Every `start()` is paired with `wait()` via the pool |

> **Requires**: PHP 8.1+, `pcntl` extension, `posix` extension (Linux/macOS — not available on Windows).

